course: dictionary
lesson: 9451
title: Standby: ready, but not off
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Standby means ready to be used or to act if needed. A TV on standby is not fully off. It is waiting, ready to turn on quickly. «TVs and other machines on standby still use electricity, so they are switched off at the wall when not in use.» The clue is still use electricity: standby is not the same as off.
explain: Standby can also be a thing or person kept ready in case it is needed, like a spare. A standby ticket is bought at the last minute if there is a free seat. Look at the words around standby to find out which meaning it has.
explain: Standby is a noun, an adjective and part of a phrasal verb. The phrasal verb stand by means to wait ready, or to support someone. Ask yourself: is standby a thing, a state, or an action? The sentence will tell you.
fact: Standby means ready to be used or to act if needed.
fact: A standby is a person or thing kept ready in case it is needed, like a spare.
fact: Standby mode: a TV or computer is switched off but still uses a little power, so it can turn on quickly.
fact: «Many devices still use electricity on standby when they look switched off.» Switching off at the plug saves energy.
fact: Stand by is a phrasal verb meaning to wait ready, or to support someone.
exercise: «Many devices still use electricity on standby when they look switched off.» What does standby mean here? | Being played loudly | *Ready to turn on quickly, still using a little power | Finished and packed away | Completely broken, with no power at all
exercise: Lily's bike has a spare tyre kept ready in case of a puncture. What is the spare tyre? | A bike that has been stolen | A puncture | A tyre that has been sold | *A standby, a spare kept ready in case it is needed
exercise: A passenger on standby waits for what? | A new phone | *A free seat | A sunny day | A parcel to arrive
test: «The ambulance crew was on standby all night, ready to go if needed.» What does on standby mean here? | Finished for the day | Stuck in traffic | *Ready to act if needed | Asleep in bed
test: Which phrase means to support someone when they need you? | stand back | *stand by | stand out | stand up
exam: According to «TVs and other machines on standby still use electricity», why should you switch them off at the wall? | Because machines get bored | *Because standby still uses power, so switching off saves energy | Because the plug needs cleaning | Because standby makes machines explode
